                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 0,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Yesterday, I met with leaders from Crisp Regional Health, including President & CEO, Steven Gautney. More than 20% of rural counties in Georgia have no doctor, or only one doctor, for the entire county. When a rural hospital closes, the closest care becomes hours away and local jobs are lost which amplifies the economic hurt close to home.\n\nCongress can do its part to make crucial investments in rural development for clean water, housing, broadband, and healthcare. But hospitals cannot stay open, and services cannot be maintained if people cannot afford healthcare.\n\nEarlier this year, the big ugly bill gutted Medicaid and Medicare. Now, Affordable Care Act tax credits \u2013 which help millions of Georgians get and keep healthcare \u2013 are ending. I will continue to fight for Georgia\u2019s families so that they have access to affordable healthcare close to home.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1763575682,
                "view_count": 185
