                "reply_count": 0,
                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "This week, I voted against a bill pushed by GOP leadership that not only failed to extend ACA tax credits, but also threatened to leave patients with less protection, destabilize the insurance market, and put Americans on the hook for big medical bills not covered by insurance.\n\nhttps://t.co/mlTvBqCbJj\n\nFortunately, several Republican House Members have joined Democrats on a discharge petition to force a vote on a bill to extend ACA tax credits. The House Speaker must call a vote but has yet to do so.\n\nYesterday, I joined my colleagues on the House steps to urge him to immediately bring this ACA tax credit extension bill to a vote.",
