                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "This month, USDA announced its Regenerative Agriculture Pilot. Interested producers should submit applications to their local NRCS office by January 15, 2026.\n\nThis program builds on the EQIP and CSP programs that our farmers have relied on for decades for soil health and reducing input costs. Middle and Southwest Georgia farmers have been a driving force for conservation efforts, benefiting from federal resources under Democratic and Republican administrations to continue to produce the highest quality, most abundant and affordable food and fiber.\n\nAs we head into 2026, I will steadfastly work in Congress to ensure these programs remain strong, transparent, and focused on real conservation outcomes that serve Georgia\u2019s farmers and families.",
